-- title:
--   Generating the level-Mp roof function field over L
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, given as a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra, let $N$, $p$, $M$ be nonzero natural numbers with $M = Np$, and let $H' \le (\mathbb{Z}/N)^{\times}$ and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ be subgroups such that $\Gamma_H(M) \le \Gamma_{H'}(N)$ as subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$; here $\Gamma_H(M) =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) is the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the set of matrices of $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower right entry, read as a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$, lies in $H$. For a subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ write $F_K(\Gamma) =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the subfield of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the set [`ModularCurve.intFormRatiosC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L83) attached to $\Gamma$, and for an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathbb{Q}((q))/\mathbb{Q}$ write [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) for the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image of $F_0$ under coefficientwise application of $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Finally [`ModularCurve.qExpand L p`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) is the ring endomorphism of $L((q))$ multiplying all exponents by $p$, i.e. $q \mapsto q^{p}$. The assertion is the equality of intermediate fields of $L((q))$
--   $$L\cdot F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_H(M)) \;\vee\; L\bigl(q\mapsto q^{p}\ \text{applied to}\ L\cdot F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_{H'}(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Np))\bigr) \;=\; L\cdot F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(Mp)),$$
--   the left-hand side being the join of the base change of $F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_H(M))$ with the field generated over $L$ by the image under $q \mapsto q^{p}$ of the base change of $F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_{H'}(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Np))$. Here $p$ is not assumed prime.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the statement that the roof $X(\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(Mp))$ of the degeneracy pair computing $U_p$ in level $M = Np$ is generated by $X_H(M)$ together with the pull-back along $\tau\mapsto p\tau$ of the level-$N$ roof $X(\Gamma_{H'}(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Np))$, over any coefficient field $L \supseteq \mathbb{Q}$. It is used in establishing the compatibility of the Hecke operator $U_p$ on level $M$ with the degeneracy maps and the Atkin–Lehner involution.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_laurentBaseChange_xHFunctionField_sup_adjoin_qExpand_xHTopFunctionFieldC.lean

